From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alex Steiner <alex@steiale.io>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 20:29:50 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 05/11] W7: bridge hardening (handle map mutex, single fd
 close, no SIGUSR2 dumper, process-wide logger)

- tunnelHandles is guarded by a mutex; every export goes through lookupHandle/storeHandle/removeHandle.
- wgTurnOn error paths: CreateTUNFromFile already closed the file, so no second unix.Close(dup); an IpcSet failure
  closes the device (which owns the fd) instead of the raw fd, and no device goroutines leak (K9).
- The SIGUSR2 goroutine dumper is removed: it indexed past its buffer on a full dump (K10).
- The logger target is one atomically swapped (func, ctx) pair. WireGuardAdapter installs it once per process
  through a static, retained sink; deinit no longer nils it (K11).
---
 Sources/WireGuardKitGo/api-apple-pf.go |  11 +--
 Sources/WireGuardKitGo/api-apple.go    | 105 +++++++++++++++----------
 2 files changed, 66 insertions(+), 50 deletions(-)

